Helios DXVK fork: dynamic-buffer discards from the local allocation cache without host-visible VRAM (opt-in)

Conduit guest/windows. Applied after 0020 by ci/windows/Build-Driver.ps1.

Each D3D11 context keeps a local allocation cache for the discard slices of
dynamic buffers (Map WRITE_DISCARD, UpdateSubresource on mappable buffers).
It is created for DEVICE_LOCAL | HOST_VISIBLE | HOST_COHERENT memory. NVK
over RM exposes no such type by default (no BAR heap, NVK_RM_BAR_MB=0), so
the cache has no memory type and every discard goes to the allocator:
allocateMemory with DEVICE_LOCAL (no type), then again without
DEVICE_LOCAL, which suballocates from the system-memory mapped pool under
the allocator's global lock; freeing the old slice on the queue thread
takes the same lock.

- d3d11: HELIOS_DXVK_LOCAL_ALLOC_CACHE_FALLBACK=1 recreates an unusable
  cache for HOST_VISIBLE system memory (the memory type those slices land in
  anyway), so discards are served from it without the allocator lock. It
  stays off by default: d3d11_mapbench frames are faster with it when the
  UMD's threaded front end is off and slower when it is on. The immediate
  context logs once which memory the cache uses.
- dxvk: allocateMemory returns before taking the allocator lock when no
  memory type matches the request (the types and heaps are fixed at device
  creation), so the DEVICE_LOCAL-first attempt of every discard that does
  not come from a cache costs no lock.

